Gravity UI 8.0.0 installed. Now:

1. `main.tsx`: import '@gravity-ui/uikit/styles/styles.css' (and fonts.css), wrap App in ThemeProvider.
2. `App.tsx`: build login page with TextInput (email, password), Checkbox, Button.

Gravity UI v8 — ThemeProvider API: `<ThemeProvider theme="light">`. Components: TextInput, PasswordInput (in v8 there's PasswordInput component? Actually Gravity UI has `PasswordInput` in @gravity-ui/uikit — yes, it exists with reveal button). Checkbox, Button.

Let me write the code. Language: user writes in Russian, so the UI text should be Russian: "Войти", "Запомнить меня", email "Электронная почта", password "Пароль".

index.css: keep page centering.

App.tsx:

```tsx
import { useState } from 'react';
import { Button, Checkbox, PasswordInput, Text, TextInput } from '@gravity-ui/uikit';

export function App() {
  const [email, setEmail] = useState('');
  const [password, setPassword] = useState('');
  const [remember, setRemember] = useState(false);

  const handleSubmit = (e: React.FormEvent) => {
    e.preventDefault();
  };

  return (
    <main className="page">
      <form className="login-card" onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
        <Text variant="header-1">Вход</Text>
        <TextInput
          type="email"
          size="l"
          placeholder="Электронная почта"
          value={email}
          onChange={(e) => setEmail(e.target.value)}
        />
        <PasswordInput ... />
        <Checkbox checked={remember} onUpdate={setRemember} content="Запомнить меня" />
        <Button view="action" size="l" width="max" type="submit">Войти</Button>
      </form>
    </main>
  );
}
```

Gravity UI Checkbox: has `content` prop or children. onUpdate receives boolean. Also onChange works.

Add CSS for .login-card: width 360px, display flex column gap, using g-spacing variables. Since Gravity UI sets body class for theme, root class "g-root" etc. ThemeProvider handles that by default in v6+ (adds classes to body by default? ThemeProvider adds classes to document body by default `rootClassName`... Actually ThemeProvider in v6 adds classes to body by default — yes, by default it applies to `body`).

index.css: body margin 0, .page grid center, background using var(--g-color-base-background).

